.TH VPG 1 "August 2026" "vpg 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vpg \- secure PostgreSQL backup and recovery for Docker containers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vpg
.B backup
.I output-directory
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B vpg
.B restore
.IR backup-directory | archive.tar.gz
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B vpg
.B verify
.IR backup-directory | archive.tar.gz
.br
.B vpg
.B list
.RI [ backup-directory ]
.br
.B vpg
.B help
.RI [command]
.br
.B vpg
.B version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vpg
(Void PostgreSQL) is a secure backup and disaster-recovery CLI for
PostgreSQL containers managed by Docker. It creates validated logical
cluster backups with integrity checks, metadata manifests, optional
compression, and guarded credential handling. Restoration performs a
full-cluster replacement only after the backup has been verified.
.PP
.B vpg
is intended for reliable backup, verification, and disaster-recovery
workflows. It performs logical backups and is not a point-in-time recovery
or physical replication solution.
.PP
Backups are written to a private incomplete directory and published only
after dumps, structure, inventory, and checksums pass validation. Failed
work is preserved for diagnosis and is never accepted by
.B verify
or
.BR restore .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B backup
Create and validate a full logical cluster backup of a running PostgreSQL
container. Produces a backup directory and optionally a
.B .tar.gz
archive with a
.B .sha256
sidecar.
.TP
.B restore
Replace a target container's PostgreSQL cluster from a completed VPG
backup directory or archive. This is destructive: the target PGDATA
contents are permanently deleted after confirmation.
.TP
.B verify
Verify backup structure, file inventory, and SHA-256 checksums for a
backup directory or archive. Archives are checked for unsafe paths and
optional sidecar checksums before contents are validated.
.TP
.B list
List complete VPG backups found in
.I backup-directory
(default: current directory). Incomplete or invalid backups are omitted.
.TP
.B help
Show top-level help, or command-specific help when a command name is given.
.TP
.B version
Print the installed VPG version.
.SH BACKUP OPTIONS
.TP
.I output-directory
Secure directory where backups will be stored. Created with mode
.B 0700
when missing. Must be owned by the current user and must not be writable
by group or others unless
.B \-\-allow\-insecure\-permissions
is used.
.TP
.BI \-\-container " name"
Running PostgreSQL Docker container name or ID.
Default:
.BR infra_postgres .
A legacy positional form
.BI "vpg backup " container " " output-directory
is also accepted.
.TP
.BI \-\-env\-file " path"
Load configuration from a dotenv file. Default:
.B ./.env
when it exists. Unless
.B \-\-allow\-insecure\-permissions
is set, the file must be owned by the current user and not accessible by
group or others.
.TP
.BI \-\-username " username"
Override
.BR POSTGRES_USER .
.TP
.BI \-\-password " password"
Override
.BR POSTGRES_PASSWORD .
This may expose the password through shell history or process arguments.
Prefer
.B \-\-password\-file
or
.BR \-\-password\-stdin .
.TP
.BI \-\-password\-file " path"
Read the PostgreSQL password from a protected regular file owned by the
current user with mode not accessible by group or others.
.TP
.B \-\-password\-stdin
Read the PostgreSQL password from standard input.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " host"
Override
.BR POSTGRES_HOST .
Default:
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.BI \-\-port " port"
Override
.BR POSTGRES_PORT .
Default:
.BR 5432 .
.TP
.BI \-\-maintenance\-db " database"
Override
.BR POSTGRES_DB .
Default:
.BR postgres .
.TP
.BI \-\-compression " 0\-9"
PostgreSQL custom-format compression level.
Default:
.BR 6 .
.TP
.B \-\-archive
Also create a
.B .tar.gz
archive. The backup directory remains available.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-archive
Disable archive creation.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-role\-passwords
Include PostgreSQL role password hashes in
.BR globals.sql .
Disabled by default. Treat such backups as secrets.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-tablespaces
Include PostgreSQL tablespace definitions.
Disabled by default.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable verbose PostgreSQL backup output.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-insecure\-permissions
Allow group/other-readable env files and group/other-writable output
directories. Prefer fixing permissions instead.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show backup help.
.SH RESTORE OPTIONS
.TP
.IR backup-directory | archive.tar.gz
Completed VPG backup directory or archive produced by
.BR "vpg backup" .
.TP
.BI \-\-container " name"
Target PostgreSQL container.
Default:
.BR infra_postgres .
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
Readiness timeout per startup phase.
Default:
.BR 240 .
Maximum:
.BR 3600 .
.TP
.B \-\-force
Skip the interactive
.B REPLACE
confirmation. Required for non-interactive restores.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-failed
Keep the isolated restore container after failure for investigation.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable verbose
.B pg_restore
output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show restore help.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration precedence for
.B backup
is:
.IP 1. 4
CLI options
.IP 2.
Current process environment
.IP 3.
Dotenv file
.IP 4.
Built-in defaults
.PP
Supported dotenv and environment variables:
.IP \[bu] 2
.B POSTGRES_USER
.IP \[bu]
.B POSTGRES_PASSWORD
.IP \[bu]
.B POSTGRES_HOST
.IP \[bu]
.B POSTGRES_PORT
.IP \[bu]
.B POSTGRES_DB
.IP \[bu]
.B BACKUP_COMPRESSION
.IP \[bu]
.B BACKUP_CREATE_ARCHIVE
.IP \[bu]
.B BACKUP_INCLUDE_ROLE_PASSWORDS
.IP \[bu]
.B BACKUP_INCLUDE_TABLESPACES
.SH BACKUP FORMAT
Each completed backup directory contains:
.IP \[bu] 2
.B manifest.txt
\- backup metadata and format version
.IP \[bu]
.B globals.sql
\- roles and optionally tablespaces
.IP \[bu]
.B database\-map.tsv
\- mapping from dump files to Base64 database names
.IP \[bu]
.B database_NNNN.dump
\- one custom-format dump per database
.IP \[bu]
.B FILES.txt
\- protected file inventory
.IP \[bu]
.B SHA256SUMS
\- checksums for inventory files
.IP \[bu]
.B BACKUP_COMPLETE
\- completion marker
.PP
With
.BR \-\-archive ,
.B vpg
also creates
.I backup-id\fB.tar.gz\fR
and
.IR backup-id\fB.tar.gz.sha256\fR .
.SH RESTORE SAFETY
Before changing the target,
.B restore
verifies the bundle format, completion state, inventory, checksums,
database map entries, Docker access, target image, PGDATA path, and
PostgreSQL major versions.
.PP
After confirmation,
.B restore
stops the target, clears its PGDATA volume, restores into a temporary
container with networking disabled, verifies database count, then starts
the original target container. If a failure occurs after PGDATA is cleared,
the target remains stopped.
.PP
Restore supports the same or a newer PostgreSQL major version than the
backup. Test major-version upgrades separately before relying on them in
production.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Create a backup with archive:
.nf
vpg backup /srv/backups/postgres \\
  \-\-container infra_postgres \\
  \-\-archive
.fi
.TP
List and verify backups:
.nf
vpg list /srv/backups/postgres
vpg verify /srv/backups/postgres/postgres_cluster_2026\-08\-16_17\-30\-00_UTC_abcd1234
vpg verify /srv/backups/postgres/postgres_cluster_2026\-08\-16_17\-30\-00_UTC_abcd1234.tar.gz
.fi
.TP
Restore from an archive (interactive confirmation):
.nf
vpg restore /srv/backups/postgres/postgres_cluster_2026\-08\-16_17\-30\-00_UTC_abcd1234.tar.gz \\
  \-\-container infra_postgres
.fi
.TP
Non-interactive restore for automation:
.nf
vpg restore ./backup.tar.gz \\
  \-\-container infra_postgres \\
  \-\-force
.fi
.TP
Backup using a password file:
.nf
vpg backup /srv/backups/postgres \\
  \-\-container infra_postgres \\
  \-\-username backup_user \\
  \-\-password\-file /run/secrets/postgres_backup_password \\
  \-\-archive
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
General failure (missing dependencies, validation failure, Docker error,
restore failure, and similar).
.TP
2
Invalid command-line usage.
.TP
130
Interrupted by signal.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B POSTGRES_USER
PostgreSQL username used for backup connections.
.TP
.B POSTGRES_PASSWORD
PostgreSQL password. Prefer
.B \-\-password\-file
or
.B \-\-password\-stdin
when possible.
.TP
.B POSTGRES_HOST
Host used inside the container for backup connections.
.TP
.B POSTGRES_PORT
Port used inside the container for backup connections.
.TP
.B POSTGRES_DB
Maintenance database used for metadata queries.
.TP
.B BACKUP_COMPRESSION
Default compression level for
.BR backup .
.TP
.B BACKUP_CREATE_ARCHIVE
Default archive creation setting
.RB ( true / false ).
.TP
.B BACKUP_INCLUDE_ROLE_PASSWORDS
Include role password hashes by default
.RB ( true / false ).
.TP
.B BACKUP_INCLUDE_TABLESPACES
Include tablespace definitions by default
.RB ( true / false ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./.env
Optional dotenv file loaded by
.B backup
when present.
.TP
.I PREFIX/bin/vpg
Installed executable symlink.
.TP
.I PREFIX/lib/vpg/
Installed VPG scripts.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/man/man1/vpg.1
Installed manual page.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.IP \[bu] 2
Linux with Bash 4.3 or newer
.IP \[bu]
Docker Engine and permission to manage the target container
.IP \[bu]
GNU core utilities:
.BR awk (1),
.BR base64 (1),
.BR find (1),
.BR sha256sum (1),
.BR sort (1),
.BR tar (1)
.IP \[bu]
A PostgreSQL-compatible container image providing
.BR psql ,
.BR pg_dump ,
.BR pg_dumpall ,
.BR pg_restore ,
and
.B pg_isready
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
When a failure has a known remediation,
.B vpg
prints a
.B "Suggested fix"
block containing the command to run.
.TP
.B "Output directory must not be writable by group or others"
Restrict the directory, for example
.BR "chmod 0700 /srv/backups/postgres" .
.TP
.B "Output directory must be owned by UID N"
Take ownership using the suggested
.BR chown (1)
command.
.TP
Windows-backed and network mounts
Paths under
.I /mnt
in WSL, along with FAT, exFAT, NTFS, and SMB mounts, report a fixed
permission mode that
.BR chmod (1)
cannot change. Back up to a Linux-native directory instead, or pass
.B \-\-allow\-insecure\-permissions
to accept the risk. In this case
.B vpg
suggests a concrete native path.
.TP
.B "Password file must not be accessible by group or others"
Run
.B chmod 0600
on the file, or avoid the file entirely with
.BR \-\-password\-stdin .
Note that
.B \-\-allow\-insecure\-permissions
deliberately does not relax secret handling.
